    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm taking the Eurostar from St Pancras to Paris next week for work. I have a couple of really large suitcases, like heavy checked bags. What are the specific weight and size limits for luggage on Eurostar? Also, how early do I actually need to be at the station for check-in/security? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar has a luggage weight limit of 30kg per bag, with a weight limit of 725kg in total for a standard seat class and 865kg for 2nd and 3rd crew class tickets. Baggage dimensions should not exceed 62cm in each direction and not exceed a height of 262cm with wheels. You must arrive at the station at least 60 minutes before departure for check-in and security screening. For the return journey, make sure to arrive 90 minutes before departure to avoid any inconvenience. Safe travels!",
